would be far worse than my own.

178
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,580
How sad he must be,

179
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:38,577
wondering if we betrayed him,

180
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:43,380
wondering if our promise was alive, yet
still waiting for us in the same place.

181
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,480
You're right, but...

182
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:52,257
The name of that friend that we left at
the Cape swearing to meet again is...

183
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:53,170
Laboon.

184
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,860
He was just a child.

185
00:08:56,220 --> 00:09:00,097
We simply couldn't take such a young
whale on a dangerous journey like that.

186
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,010
A whale?

187
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:03,470
Yes.

188
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:23,060
I can only imagine how
big he's grown since then

189
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,840
You think that whale
understood your promise?

190
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:29,280
In his own way

191
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:33,377
I can't help but think that he's
still waiting for us at that cape?

192
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:36,000
staring longingly at the Grand Line.

193
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:42,580
He probably wants to hear us play our
cheerful music again, dancing and singing.

194
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:46,522
Although, I suppose it's
a bit late for that now.

195
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,200
Even if I am able to return,

196
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:53,440
I don't think he'll forgive us for
running away and dying like that.

197
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,817
But no matter how much he resents me?

198
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,547
For forcing him to suffer
all of these years,

199
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:03,180
death is never an apology!

200
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:10,285
Because when a man makes a promise he
doesn't stop fighting until he fulfills it.

201
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:15,640
So there you have it
that's it the whole story.

202
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:24,400
This is crazy what are the
chances I'll be damned?

203
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,537
We've met that whale before,

204
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:37,557
and

205
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:41,897
we know

206
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:43,460
that promise.

207
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:56,360
You know him that's crazy
how is that possible

208
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:01,980
It was when we passed through to
the Grand Line at the two capes

209
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:05,560
The damn giant whale was
blocking the entrance

210
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,997
It was at the Red Line Grief drove him to

211
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:13,677
